---
layout: null
---
{%- comment -%}
  THE SITEMAP, WITH A LAST-MODIFIED DATE WHEREVER THE REPOSITORY STORES ONE.

  jekyll-sitemap writes its own sitemap only when the site has none, so this file replaces the
  plugin's template and nothing else: the plugin still writes robots.txt, which names this file.
  The URL set is the plugin's, rule for rule: every output collection document, every HTML page,
  and every static .htm / .html / .xhtml / .pdf file, each unless its front matter says
  sitemap: false, and never /404.html. scripts/ci/verify_publication_hygiene.py reads the result.

  WHY. The plugin dates a page only from a last_modified_at field no page here carries, so 5 of
  1,769 URLs had a date and a crawler could not tell a patch page that changed yesterday from one
  untouched since 2019.

  WHERE A DATE COMES FROM. Only from stored data, never from the clock and never from a file's
  modification time (on the deploy runner that is the checkout time, which is the build time):
    - a patch record: its record_last_updated, the moment a writer last changed the record, or
      the release date update_published_at for the few records that store no record_last_updated;
    - a product, company or version tracker: the newest record_last_updated among the records
      the tracker lists (same product_id, company_id, or product_id and update_version);
    - a post or other collection document: its last_modified_at, or the date its front matter or
      file name states. Jekyll gives a document with no date of its own the build time as its
      date, which is why /about/ and /articles/ used to carry the moment of the last deploy as
      their lastmod; a date equal to the build time is not a stored date and is not printed;
    - any other page: its last_modified_at when the front matter states one.
  A URL with no stored date gets no lastmod element. That is the honest reading of "unknown":
  the homepage, the Patch Feed pages and the methodology page are in that group, and so is
  every static file, whose only date is the file time this template refuses to print.

  A STORED VALUE THAT IS NOT A DATE NEVER STOPS THE BUILD AND NEVER PRINTS. A record is written by
  several lanes and by hand, and nothing validates these fields before the build. Every candidate
  passes the same three tests before it is compared or printed, and a value that fails one simply
  leaves its URL without a lastmod:
    - it is written as a date: four characters, then a hyphen (so the bare word a date filter
      reads as "the present moment", and a bare number it reads as seconds since 1970, are not);
    - the standard date filter can read it. That filter returns what it was given when it cannot,
      so the seconds it yields are then no date at all and fall under the floor below, which is
      the first second of the year 2000 and predates every release tracked here;
    - it is not later than this build. A page cannot have changed in the future.
  The date is printed with the same standard filter, which cannot raise. Jekyll's
  date_to_xmlschema is deliberately not used here: it raises on a value it cannot read, and one
  malformed stamp on one of 1,600 records would then fail every deploy until someone repaired it.

  Written in plain Liquid (no where_exp, no group_by) so scripts/tests/test_publication_hygiene.py
  [SM] can render this very file with the Liquid gem and pin each rule above.
{%- endcomment -%}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9 http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9/sitemap.xsd" xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
{%- assign sm_floor = 946684800 -%}
{%- assign sm_now = site.time | date: '%s' | plus: 0 -%}
{%- for sm_collection in site.collections -%}
{%- if sm_collection.output != false -%}
{%- for sm_doc in sm_collection.docs -%}
{%- if sm_doc.sitemap != false -%}
{%- assign sm_lastmod = sm_doc.last_modified_at | default: '' -%}
{%- if sm_lastmod == '' and sm_doc.date and sm_doc.date != site.time -%}{%- assign sm_lastmod = sm_doc.date -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign sm_shape = sm_lastmod | append: '' | slice: 4, 1 -%}
{%- assign sm_seconds = sm_lastmod | date: '%s' | plus: 0 -%}
{%- assign sm_dated = false -%}
{%- if sm_shape == '-' and sm_seconds >= sm_floor and sm_seconds <= sm_now -%}{%- assign sm_dated = true -%}{%- endif %}
<url>
<loc>{{ sm_doc.url | replace: '/index.html', '/' | absolute_url | xml_escape }}</loc>
{%- if sm_dated %}
<lastmod>{{ sm_lastmod | date: '%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%:z' }}</lastmod>
{%- endif %}
</url>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign sm_records = site.html_pages | where: 'update_entry', true -%}
{%- for sm_page in site.html_pages -%}
{%- if sm_page.sitemap != false and sm_page.url != '/404.html' -%}
{%- assign sm_lastmod = '' -%}
{%- if sm_page.update_entry == true -%}
  {%- assign sm_lastmod = sm_page.record_last_updated | default: sm_page.update_published_at | default: '' -%}
{%- elsif sm_page.layout == 'aux-patch-product' or sm_page.layout == 'aux-patch-company' or sm_page.layout == 'aux-patch-version' -%}
  {%- assign sm_listed = '' | split: '' -%}
  {%- if sm_page.layout == 'aux-patch-company' -%}
    {%- assign sm_key = sm_page.company_id | default: '' | append: '' -%}
    {%- if sm_key != '' -%}{%- assign sm_listed = sm_records | where: 'company_id', sm_key -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign sm_key = sm_page.product_id | default: '' | append: '' -%}
    {%- if sm_key != '' -%}{%- assign sm_listed = sm_records | where: 'product_id', sm_key -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- assign sm_version = '' -%}
  {%- if sm_page.layout == 'aux-patch-version' -%}
    {%- assign sm_version = sm_page.update_version | default: '' | append: '' -%}
    {%- if sm_version == '' -%}{%- assign sm_listed = '' | split: '' -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- assign sm_newest = 0 -%}
  {%- for sm_record in sm_listed -%}
    {%- assign sm_stamp = sm_record.record_last_updated | default: '' -%}
    {%- if sm_version != '' -%}
      {%- assign sm_record_version = sm_record.update_version | default: '' | append: '' -%}
      {%- if sm_record_version != sm_version -%}{%- assign sm_stamp = '' -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- assign sm_shape = sm_stamp | append: '' | slice: 4, 1 -%}
    {%- assign sm_seconds = sm_stamp | date: '%s' | plus: 0 -%}
    {%- if sm_shape == '-' and sm_seconds >= sm_floor and sm_seconds <= sm_now and sm_seconds > sm_newest -%}
      {%- assign sm_newest = sm_seconds -%}{%- assign sm_lastmod = sm_stamp -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- elsif sm_page.last_modified_at -%}
  {%- assign sm_lastmod = sm_page.last_modified_at -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign sm_shape = sm_lastmod | append: '' | slice: 4, 1 -%}
{%- assign sm_seconds = sm_lastmod | date: '%s' | plus: 0 -%}
{%- assign sm_dated = false -%}
{%- if sm_shape == '-' and sm_seconds >= sm_floor and sm_seconds <= sm_now -%}{%- assign sm_dated = true -%}{%- endif %}
<url>
<loc>{{ sm_page.url | replace: '/index.html', '/' | absolute_url | xml_escape }}</loc>
{%- if sm_dated %}
<lastmod>{{ sm_lastmod | date: '%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%:z' }}</lastmod>
{%- endif %}
</url>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- for sm_file in site.static_files -%}
{%- if sm_file.extname == '.htm' or sm_file.extname == '.html' or sm_file.extname == '.xhtml' or sm_file.extname == '.pdf' -%}
{%- unless sm_file.sitemap == false or sm_file.name == '404.html' %}
<url>
<loc>{{ sm_file.path | replace: '/index.html', '/' | absolute_url | xml_escape }}</loc>
</url>
{%- endunless -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor %}
</urlset>
